<%# The in-app route to the legal pages (story 0016).

    App Review guideline 5.1.1(i) requires the privacy policy to be reachable
    from inside the app, not only from the App Store Connect metadata field. The
    listing link alone is a rejection.

    Why here and not a site-wide footer: the two screens that already end in a
    `.coda` are the reader's own room and the archive, both of which a person
    arrives at deliberately and leaves at their own pace. The daily page is not
    one of them on purpose — DESIGN.md rule 5 keeps nothing between the reader
    and the artwork, and `caps-link-row-costs-44px` says every row of these costs
    a full 44px on a screen already measured tight against the fold.

    One partial rather than two copies, because the pair will grow (terms, an
    about line) and two codas drifting apart is how a legal link goes missing
    from one screen for six months. %>
<nav class="legal" aria-label="About this app">
  <%= link_to "Privacy", privacy_path, class: "caps-link" %>
  <%= link_to "Support", support_path, class: "caps-link" %>
</nav>
